{title: 423 - Glorious Things of Thee Are Spoken}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #423 • AUSTRIA • 13.15.15.16}
{lyricist: John Newton}
{composer: F. Joseph Haydn}
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 423}
{meta: tune AUSTRIA}
{meta: meter 13.15.15.16}
{meta: category Doctrines - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Glorious things [Bb]of [Eb]thee [Bb7]are spoken, [Gm]Zion, [Bb7/D]cityof [Adim]ourGod;
[Eb]He whose word [Bb]cannot [Eb]be [Bb7]broken [Ab]Formed [Gm]thee [Bb7/D]for [Eb]His [Fm/Ab]own [Adim]a bode;
[Bb]On [Eb/Bb]the [Bb]Rock of A [Bb7/D]ges [Eb]founded, [Bb7/Ab]What [Gm]can [Bb7/Ab]shake [Cm]thy sure [F7]repose?
[Eb/G]With salvation's [Ab]wall [Bb7/F]surrounded, Thou mayest [Eb/G]smile [Ab]at [Eb/Bb]all [Bb7]thy foes.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]See the [Bb7/D]streams of [Eb]living waters
[Eb]Springing [Bb7/D]from eternal [Adim]love,
[Eb]Well supply [Bb7]thy [Eb]sons [Gm]and [Eb]daughters,
[Eb]And all [Bb7/D]fear and [Ab]want [Eb]remove;
[Bb]Who can faint [Eb]when [Bb]such [Gm]a [Cm]river
[Bb]Ever flows [Eb]their [Bb]thirst [Gm]to [Cm]assuage?
[Eb/G]Grace, [Ab]which, like [Bb7/F]the Lord, [Eb/G]the [Ab]Giver,
[Eb/G]Never [Ab]fails [Eb]from [Bb7/Ab]age [Ab]to [Bb7]age.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]Round each [Bb]habitation [Bb7/D]hovering,
[Eb]See the [Bb7/D]cloud and [Ab]fire [Eb]appear
[Eb]For a [Bb]glory [Bb7]and [Ab]a [Bb7/D]covering,
[Eb]Showing [Bb7/D]that the [Ab]Lord [Eb]is [Adim]near;
[Bb]Blest inhabitants [Cm]of [F7]Zion,
[Bb]Washed in the Redeemer's [F7]blood;
[Eb/G]Jesus, [Ab]whom [Bb7/F]their souls [Eb/G]rely [Bb7]on,
[Eb/G]Makes [Ab]them [Bb7/F]kings and [Eb/G]priests [Ab]to [Bb7]God.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Eb]Savior, [Bb7/D]if of [Ab]Zion's [Eb]city
[Eb]I, through [Bb7/D]grace, a [Ab]member [Adim]am,
[Eb]Let the [Bb7/D]world deride [Gm]or [Eb]pity,
[Eb]I will [Bb7/D]glory [Ab]in [Eb]Thy [Adim]name;
[Bb]Fading is [Eb]the [Bb]worldling's [Cm]pleasure,
[Bb]All his boasted [Bb7/Ab]pomp [Cm]and [F7]show;
[Eb/G]Solid [Ab]joys [Bb7/F]and lasting [Ab]treasure
[Eb/G]None but [Bb7/F]Zion's children [Eb/Bb]know.
{end_of_verse}
